WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.300
How can a listening session inform a decision without overpromising?

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:08.600
Give the conversation a clear purpose and an honest boundary.

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:14.000
Before inviting people, explain what is open to change, what is fixed,

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:16.250
and who makes the decision.

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:20.300
Listening is not a promise to adopt every suggestion.

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:25.289
During the session, invite different accounts and ask neutral follow-up questions.

00:00:25.289 --> 00:00:30.732
A quiet room does not necessarily mean agreement, and the loudest voice

00:00:30.732 --> 00:00:33.000
is not the whole community.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:37.154
Afterward, distinguish what people said from the team’s interpretation.

00:00:37.154 --> 00:00:42.231
Note whose perspectives were heard and the limits of the session.

00:00:42.231 --> 00:00:45.000
It is not a representative poll.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:46.778
Then close the loop.

00:00:46.778 --> 00:00:51.222
Explain what happens next and how input will be considered.

00:00:51.222 --> 00:00:56.556
A clear update can connect the conversation to the organization’s actual decision

00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:57.000
process.

